      "id": 1,
      "text": "Locust Fork got its name when General Andrew Jackson carved his name into a locust tree during a 1813 encampment along the river.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Locust_Fork%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s high‑school football stadium, Gary Pate Field, honors a former Locust Fork coach who led the team to many victories.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Locust_Fork%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Locust Fork was officially incorporated on January 18, 1977, marking its transition from a rural community to an incorporated municipality.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Locust_Fork%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town sits atop a bluff overlooking the Blackburn Fork of the Little Warrior River, offering scenic views of the surrounding valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Locust_Fork%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "For a century, Locust Fork’s surrounding hills were mined for coal, though no active mining operations exist today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Locust_Fork%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
